From: EasyStick maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] sdio: log TX dequeue and slave-buffer drops

0018 closed 4-way. The following gwping run queued Linux TX (wlan0
TX 4 then 7) but logged no CMD53_TX after ip addr add. SET_IP 0xD
timed out with no 0d 02. Gateway ARP stayed incomplete. CMD53_TX is
emitted only after is_sdio_write_buffer_available succeeds, so a
silent kfree on BUFFER_UNAVAILABLE is indistinguishable from a stuck
tx_process thread.

Log the first 24 dequeues and the first 16 buffer drops (then every
32nd). Do not change ACK, queueing, or C6 commands.

What this cannot see: whether C6 put a frame on air after a successful
CMD53_TX. The negative tests are: boot has no 254x status=0x00000000
storm; cold 4-way still has msg3 00 97 and two 08 02; after ip addr
add the log shows either TX dq plus CMD53_TX, or TX dq plus
TX drop no-buf, or neither.

---
--- a/sdio/esp_sdio.c
+++ b/sdio/esp_sdio.c
@@ -875,7 +875,13 @@
 		buf_available -= buf_needed;
 
 	if (!retry) {
-		/* No buffer available at slave */
+		static unsigned drop_n;
+
+		drop_n++;
+		if (drop_n <= 16 || !(drop_n % 32))
+			esp_info("TX drop no-buf n=%u need=%u avail=%u host_count=%u\n",
+				 drop_n, buf_needed, buf_available,
+				 context->tx_buffer_count);
 		return BUFFER_UNAVAILABLE;
 	}
 
@@ -941,6 +947,23 @@
 		if (atomic_read(&tx_pending))
 			atomic_dec(&tx_pending);
 
+		{
+			static unsigned dq;
+			struct esp_payload_header *th =
+				(struct esp_payload_header *)tx_skb->data;
+
+			dq++;
+			if (dq <= 24 || !(dq % 32))
+				esp_info("TX dq n=%u len=%u if=%u type=%u qh=%d qm=%d ql=%d pend=%d\n",
+					 dq, tx_skb->len,
+					 th ? th->if_type : 99,
+					 th ? th->packet_type : 99,
+					 atomic_read(&queue_items[PRIO_Q_HIGH]),
+					 atomic_read(&queue_items[PRIO_Q_MID]),
+					 atomic_read(&queue_items[PRIO_Q_LOW]),
+					 atomic_read(&tx_pending));
+		}
+
 		retry = MAX_WRITE_RETRIES;
 
 		/* resume network tx queue if bearable load */
